==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From [[Middle English]] ''tan(c)kard(e)'', denoting 'a large tub for carrying liquid', perhaps related to Dutch ''tanckaert'' ([https://en.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/tankard ''Oxford Dictionaries'']), meaning the same thing, but both of unknown origin. <br/>The notion that the word comes from  ''Tanquard'' is wholly untenable (see [http://dmnes.org/name/Tanquard ''The Dictionary of Medieval Names from European Sources''] and [https://books.google.com.br/books?id=0AyDDQAAQBAJ&pg=PA2624&dq=The+Oxford+Dictionary+of+Family+Names+tankard&hl=pt-BR&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjHnIKz9N_gAhWHUt8KHYHqBAYQ6AEIKTAA#v=onepage&q=The%20Oxford%20Dictionary%20of%20Family%20Names%20tankard&f=false ''The Oxford Dictionary of Family Names in Britain and Ireland'']). Meaning "drinking vessel" is first recorded late 15th century.

